;; The print level's divergences (doc/C23-SURVEY.md, "As built: C3b"; bin/repr-c roundtrip): the classes of
;; test/repr/c/roundtrip-known.edn, in test/goi/divergences.edn's format (C8, generated from its :classes). A case is "corpus file", its
;; reason "known CLASS: the class's text".
;; No class takes `unclassified`, the placeholder an older --record gave a new failing file: bin/reap reports such a file as
;; in no class (queue 122); since 2026-11-02 --record writes none (it prints the file and fails). Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :cc-grammar
  :title "the reference accepts the file, the port's parser (cc's, C3's trees) does not"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the reference accepts the file, the port's parser (cc's, C3's trees) does not: C23's attributes in positions cc's grammar lacks, the parenthesized storage-class compound literal, _Decimal64x, a declaration gcc's dialect takes (CS40 (a)'s rule; deferred to C4 and C7, CS80)"
  :decided "CS80 (a); C8"
  :match [#"^known cc-grammar:"]}
 {:id :converter-gap
  :title "a construct the converter does not write or writes losing a part"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "a construct the converter does not write or writes losing a part: an octal _BitInt or d32 suffix, a function defined through a typedef or auto, __declspec, an empty literal's digits, an attribute list after a declarator's comma, nullptr as a case label's operand (CS83), C2y's if and switch declarations, read as a block that declares them and printed as that block (CS194 (a))"
  :decided "CS83 (a); C8"
  :match [#"^known converter-gap:"]}
 {:id :eval-limits
  :title "the evaluated port's limits (CS60, CS78)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the evaluated port's limits (CS60, CS78): a recursion deeper than the evaluator's 10,000 calls (a stack overflow), or a read past the round trip's budget (REPR_C_READ_BUDGET, 120 s; a third of it for the :full read's): deferred until C5 compiles repr/c"
  :decided "CS60 (a), CS78 (a); C8"
  :match [#"^known eval-limits:"]}
 {:id :macro-context
  :title "a recovered invocation or a printed expansion means another thing where the print stands"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "a recovered invocation or a printed expansion means another thing where the print stands: a name a later function-like macro takes (the original's tokens hidden from it), an invocation's stringized escapes and spacing (CS82)"
  :decided "CS82 (b) in C5, (a) until then (the user, 2026-10-30): a fix planned; deferred (the user, 2026-11-02, queue 122 F5)"
  :match [#"^known macro-context:"]}
 {:id :objects
  :title "the print is the same program (levels 1, 2, 4) but gcc -O0's object code differs: an asm label's section"
  :kind :design
  :why "the print is the same program (levels 1, 2, 4) but gcc -O0's object code differs by an asm label's section (builtins/memops-asm.c, strstr-asm.c): CS81 (a), level 4 the judge for them"
  :decided "CS81 (a) for the rest (the user, 2026-10-30)"
  :match [#"^known objects:"]}
 {:id :objects-macro-body
  :title "the print is the same program (levels 1, 2, 4) but gcc -O0's object code differs: code an invocation made"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "gcc -O0 gives every token of one expansion the invocation's location, and drops the nop before a body's end when its last statement and its brace share it; since 2026-11-06 (CS274 (a)) the print writes an invocation that made several top-level items or several statements of a list as the invocation itself (:c/macro-stmt on the first form, :c/macro-part on the rest), and 24 of the 26 files pass; left: inflate.c (zlib's statement macros inside larger statements), pr27528.c (its asm operands' constants)"
  :decided "CS81 (b) for the bodies an invocation made (the user, 2026-10-30; queue 122 F5); CS274 (a) (the user, 2026-11-06)"
  :match [#"^known objects-macro-body:"]}
 {:id :print-grammar
  :title "the :lines print holds what cc's grammar (the reread) or gcc refuses though the original did not"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the :lines print holds what cc's grammar (the reread) or gcc refuses though the original did not: an attribute leading a type name, a recovered invocation of a pp-number with a UCN, a ref to #embed's resource the print's directory lacks (CS80)"
  :decided "CS80 (a); C8"
  :match [#"^known print-grammar:"]}
 {:id :reexpansion
  :title "a macro invocation inside a larger one is printed expanded, and reexpanded by the reread"
  :kind :design
  :why "a macro invocation inside a larger one (not a whole node) is printed expanded, and a self-referential macro of the expansion (musl's #define stdout (stdout)) is expanded again by the reread: the forms gain the inner invocation's :c/macro (N6's limit; the objects equal)"
  :decided "CS262 (a); C8"
  :match [#"^known reexpansion:"]}
 {:id :run-address
  :title "the original and the print run differently though their objects are equal"
  :kind :design
  :why "the original and the print run differently though their objects are equal: the program prints addresses (return-addr.c), a run's own nondeterminism"
  :decided "CS262 (a); C8"
  :match [#"^known run-address:"]}
 {:id :self-include
  :title "the main file includes itself (#include __FILE__-like tests)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the main file includes itself (#include __FILE__-like tests): its tokens are the main file's twice, refused by the converter"
  :decided "CS261 (a): deferred, the converter to read the re-entered main file as an include of its own (the user, 2026-11-02, queue 122 F5)"
  :match [#"^known self-include:"]}
 {:id :split-declaration
  :title "a declaration begins in one file and ends in another (SPEC §4.3's split-declaration)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "a declaration begins in one file and ends in another (SPEC §4.3's split-declaration): refused; since 2026-11-06 (CS275 (a)) not when every other file's token comes from an #include the declaration holds between the items of a statement list (the print writes the #include there: 18_include, zlib's infback and inflate); left: an #include inside an initializer or an enumeration (quickjs's libregexp.c, unicode_gen.c)"
  :decided "CS104 (a): the converter keeps such a declaration whole (C6); deferred as at eval (the user, 2026-11-02, queue 122 F5)"
  :match [#"^known split-declaration:"]}
]
